--TEST--
`stats` is the one member of § 1's four asked about a whole queue, so a receipt is not something it takes — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members` and `rule:concurrency/attempts-are-finite-and-a-dead-letter-is-kept`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `cancel` and `status` are about one row and take the receipt that names it.
// `stats` is about a population — § 6 asks for the dead-letter table to be
// watched, and a table is not watched one job at a time — so what it takes is
// the queue's own name, the same string `push`'s `queue` option carries.
var $counts = Core\Queue::stats("default");

uint $pending = $counts->pending();
uint $claimed = $counts->claimed();
uint $attempts = $counts->attempts();
uint $dead = $counts->deadLettered();
uint $buried = $counts->deadAttempts();

// So the two arguments are not interchangeable in either direction, and this
// is the direction a caller reaches for by habit after holding a receipt.
var $receipt = Core\Queue::push("jobs/send-receipt.nvs");
var $wrong = Core\Queue::stats($receipt);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `Core\Queue\Id`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
